      "final_answer": "The reservation details show that the insurance is \"no\" for this reservation. According to the policy, \"The user cannot add insurance after initial booking.\" This means I cannot add insurance to an existing reservation after it has been booked.\n\nThe user is insisting on having insurance added, but this is against policy. I need to inform the user that insurance cannot be added after the initial booking. Since this is a policy restriction that I cannot override, and the user is not accepting this (they're insisting persistently), I may need to transfer them to a human agent if they continue to insist.\n\nHowever, let me first explain the policy to the user clearly and see if they understand. If they still insist after I explain the policy, then I would need to transfer them.\n\nLet me respond to the user explaining the situation.\n</think>\n\nI've checked your reservation PEP4E0. The reservation shows that travel insurance was not purchased at the time of booking (insurance: \"no\"). \n\nAccording to airline policy, travel insurance cannot be added after the initial booking. Insurance must be purchased at the time of booking and is non-refundable once the remaining amount is used. This is a system limitation that applies to all reservations.\n\nSince you mentioned that other passengers in your family already have insurance for their flights, I understand your concern. However, I cannot add insurance to your existing reservation as it's against policy.\n\nIf you continue to insist on adding insurance despite this policy restriction, I would need to transfer you to a human agent who may be able to assist further. Would you like me to proceed with the transfer, or is there anything else I can help you with regarding your reservation?",
